<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Builder IPS Praha plans CZK 3.5 gross div.</title>
<headline>Builder IPS Praha plans CZK 3.5 gross div.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech construction firm IPS Praha a.s. said on Monday it would propose paying a 3.5 crown 1996 dividend for each share with a nominal value of 100 crowns.</p>
<p>The previous year, IPS did not pay a cash dividend, but instead paid a premium through a stock split, giving share holders 11 shares with a nominal value of 100 crowns for each original share which had a nominal value of 1,000 crowns.</p>
</text>
